# Line-ending policy.
#
# Git normalizes to LF in the repository; the working tree keeps whatever each
# file's history calls for. Without this, the checked-in endings depend on
# whichever tool last wrote the file -- an editor or script that rewrites a CRLF
# file as LF turns a small change into a whole-file rewrite, burying the real
# diff and poisoning git blame. That happened in #178, where a +33/-8 change to
# nn_unit_test.cpp was recorded as 17,011 lines, and #179 undid it by hand.
#
# With these rules the same mistake is a no-op: the index holds LF either way,
# so a tool that converts endings produces no diff, and checkout restores the
# working-tree convention.

* text=auto

# Never normalized.
*.png binary
*.pdf binary
*.golden -text

